## Verification record

One row per verified scope. The summary above is derived from these rows and never overrides them.

| Verified scope | Reviewed revision | Reviewer | Date | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|

How verification works:

- Registration records the observed pin and leaves every scope pending.
- A verified scope supports work on that scope while unrelated scopes stay pending.
- Recording a verification names the scope, reviewed revision, reviewer, date and evidence. Matching SHAs alone are not evidence.
- A change to the relevant basis — the pin, an authority in `sot.md`, or verified context content — triggers reassessment of the affected scope only.
- Coordination text (phase, in progress, next steps) does not invalidate technical verification.
- On reassessment, keep the previous row as prior evidence and add the new row; distinguish prior evidence from evidence applicable to the current task.

Update this file when a material fact changes: phase, a blocker appearing or clearing, the next action, a newly observed pin, or a verification change. Leave it unchanged otherwise.
